  "limits": [
    "Browser-reported metadata only; not a complete packet capture or other-application monitor. Headers, cookies, bodies and WebSocket frames are excluded.",
    "Native tests cover HTTP requests and responses. WebSocket handshake projection is unit-tested; browser API support is documented, but no native WebSocket fixture was run.",
    "Storage failures, restart restore, deadlines and resource/command limits are covered by unit tests; native suites cover actual observers, exports, UI and lifecycle.",
    "The initial integration unit run exposed a missing clearTimeout in the VM test environment. The fixture now pairs clearImmediate with its existing setImmediate-backed timer.",
    "The two unsuccessful Firefox attempts were fixture errors: an expression-wrapper incompatibility, then parsing an unfinished native export. Both attempts are retained; no capture logic was changed for these failures.",
    "The initial Chrome/Edge feature passes preceded a small UI optimization and layout refinement. Final passes use the matching runtime hashes.",
    "Earlier source-layout verification covers the full userscript/MCP workflows. This feature pass repeats native GM storage/HTTP with blocking and the complete blocker suites; desktop OS helpers were not repeated."
